# One-way valve, layer 1: default deny (DR-002; reversed after adversarial verification on 2026-08-24)
#
# The first design ignored only `state/` and `_private/` and tracked everything else. Verification showed why
# that was wrong: README and SETUP tell users to keep documents, notes, and tracks in this workspace, so ordinary
# paths such as `company/tracker.md` could commit company data. A denylist blocks only paths already imagined.
#
# The design was reversed: ignore everything, then restore only the engine. New files stay outside Git by
# default; engine changes are tracked deliberately. Mistakes now fail in the safer direction.
#
# Conversely, this repository does not back up instance data. Arrange that backup separately (system/CHECKLIST.md).
#
# To add an engine file, add one line to the allowlist below. That line is the decision point.

# Deny everything.
/*

# Restore only the engine.
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/SETUP.md
!/TUTORIAL.md
!/MANUAL.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/AGENTS.md
!/setup.sh
!/tools/
!/templates/
!/system/
!/.codex/
# Claude Code, Codex and Antigravity: the kit's settings and hook declaration, and the copies of the
# kit's skills that tools/skills.py writes from system/skills/. A skill folder of the owner's own
# beside them, and anything else there, belongs to the instance.
!/.claude/
/.claude/*
!/.claude/settings.json
!/.claude/skills/
/.claude/skills/*
!/.claude/skills/lenses/
!/.claude/skills/deep-pass/
!/.claude/skills/plain-writing/
!/.claude/skills/large-jobs/
!/.claude/skills/now/
!/.claude/skills/recall/
!/.claude/skills/dossier/
!/.claude/skills/garden/
!/.claude/skills/paper-to-kit/
!/.agents/
/.agents/*
!/.agents/hooks.json
!/.agents/skills/
/.agents/skills/*
!/.agents/skills/lenses/
!/.agents/skills/deep-pass/
!/.agents/skills/plain-writing/
!/.agents/skills/large-jobs/
!/.agents/skills/now/
!/.agents/skills/recall/
!/.agents/skills/dossier/
!/.agents/skills/garden/
!/.agents/skills/paper-to-kit/
!/state/
!/.github/

# Deny these paths again inside restored directories. What one installation owns is in instance/,
# which is never restored.
# An installation from before instance/ keeps its files here until `bash setup.sh --force` moves
# them, and no Git hook guards them, so these old places stay denied.
/system/memory-config.json
/system/memory-config.json.*
/system/instance-rules.md
/system/rituals.local.md
/system/decisions.md
/system/memory-map.html
/system/build-log.md
/system/debate/*
!/system/debate/README.md
# All state belongs to the instance. Keep only the directory placeholder.
/state/*
!/state/.gitkeep
# Claude local settings, including permission allowlists, belong to the machine.
/.claude/settings.local.json

# Miscellaneous.
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# An installation's own lines go below the marker: a folder of its own that Git should keep, written
# as `!/notes/`, and further ignore lines. A `git pull` merges the lines above and keeps these, and
# doctor does not count them as an engine change (KIT-DR-090).
# --- this installation's own lines ---
